      "writtenOn": "2020-09-23T18:09:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Kind of.  Everything can be considered a sub-feature in some way.\n\nIs it expected that nearly everyone who enables TRUSTY will need all these other options enabled too?  If so, default y could be okay.  But if there are substantial use cases for not having these other options enabled, then they shouldn\u0027t be enabled by default.\n\nAlso, are any of these options actually required for everyone?  Anything that is required shouldn\u0027t be an option.",
      "parentUuid": "02d3504a_6f951b2a",
      "revId": "fd046a934df2db1be0a7d63007341d89676fdce0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9bf7e29_1ef42624",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-23T18:24:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No they are not required by everyone, but there is not much point in enabling TRUSTY without any of the submodules. TRUSTY_VIRTIO and TRUSTY_VIRTIO_IPC are needed to talk to trusty, so there is not much point of skipping those. TRUSTY_IRQ is need on every device that the the corresponding entry in the device tree.",
      "parentUuid": "dbeb521d_30ae2731",
      "revId": "fd046a934df2db1be0a7d63007341d89676fdce0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
