      "writtenOn": "2020-09-23T18:57:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m just abandoning this change for now.  You\u0027ll probably continue to get complaints from people about enabling options by default, though.  Maybe some of them shouldn\u0027t really be options, which would avoid this issue.  Also maybe some of these should be boolean settings for the trusty-core module rather than separate modules.\n\nNote that regardless of this change, downstream kconfigs need to be updated to use \u003dm for GKI compatibility.  (I wonder how people were using this this driver when it wasn\u0027t GKI-compatible?)",
